       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose of 200 mg/day. I know of no protocol or indication that supports it, and in a 70 kg adult with normal organ function it would likely cause harm. I can't verify the clinical context from here, so I don't want to put an order into the system that could reach the patient.\n\nI can do any of these:\n- Enter sertraline at a standard dose, up to 200 mg once daily.\n- Enter a lower dose now and titrate. Doses are usually raised in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least one week.\n- Help with a different order if the goal is something else, such as treating a particular condition or managing an overdose.\n\nIf you think a dose above the maximum is justified, I'd suggest discussing it with clinical pharmacy and documenting your rationale. The order should go through that review rather than being entered directly.\n\nTell me how you'd like to proceed."
